-- SEED — enable `crm` on the DISPOSABLE SYNTHETIC TENANT, with a stage config.
-- Track S, 2026-09-25. Controller decision the same day: GOLDEN PATH RUN 1 MOVES TO
-- THE SYNTHETIC TENANT, because the run creates a fake lead, a fake estimate, a fake
-- job and fake purchase orders and Brothers Metal Roofing is a live client workspace.
--
-- THIS IS A DATA ROW, NOT A MIGRATION. No schema object changes. It is recorded as a
-- file anyway, because a row inserted by hand into a shared database with no file is
-- the orphan class §4.7 spent a week bounding.
--
-- WHY IT IS NOT JUST A ROW, MEASURED BEFORE ANYTHING WAS WRITTEN (all three rolled back):
--   · no `crm` row                 -> create_deal REFUSES: "organization e0851ad8… has
--                                     no crm stage config"
--   · `crm` row, config = '{}'     -> create_deal REFUSES WITH THE SAME MESSAGE. A bare
--                                     entitlement row does NOT make step 1 work.
--   · `crm` row + a stages config  -> step 1 succeeds, the lead lands at stage `new_lead`.
-- The mechanism: create_deal reads `crm_stage_config(org) -> 0 ->> 'key'` and raises when
-- it is null, and crm_stage_config_internal is `coalesce(config->'stages','[]')` over the
-- crm row — so both an absent row and an empty config produce the same null first stage.
--
-- THE CONFIG IS A SNAPSHOT OF BROTHERS METAL ROOFING's, TAKEN 2026-09-25, md5
-- 8cd45bccb736d26d6163c8bc91a81d5b — EMBEDDED LITERALLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT READ FROM
-- BMR AT RUN TIME. Reading it live would couple a disposable test tenant to a live
-- client's configuration: BMR edits a stage label and the synthetic tenant's behaviour
-- changes with nobody told. A literal snapshot can DIVERGE, which is a difference you can
-- see; a live read cannot diverge, which is a difference you cannot.
--
-- IT CARRIES NO CUSTOMER DATA, and that was checked rather than assumed: the config is 7
-- generic stage keys/labels (New Lead … Won/Lost), a follow-up cadence of [2,5], and a
-- 4-key lead_control_center (fields, checklists, command_stages, lead_type_options).
-- A scan of every string in it for phone / email / street-address shapes returned 0.
--
-- NOTHING ELSE IS ENABLED. The synthetic tenant keeps estimating + coordination + field
-- and gains crm, which is the four the twelve steps need and no more. BMR's entitlements
-- are unchanged by this file.
--
-- KNOWN CONSEQUENCE, stated rather than discovered tomorrow: the synthetic tenant's ONE
-- existing deal (a570f24c…, "SYNTHETIC Test Homeowner") sits at stage `new_scan`, which is
-- StructTech's vocabulary and is NOT one of these 7 keys — so it renders in no column on
-- the board. It is left alone on purpose: the run creates its own lead at step 1, and
-- moving this one would put a second lead in "New Lead" for Jacob to tell apart.

insert into public.tenant_modules (org_id, module_key, enabled, config)
